<title>UK: BP says agrees North Sea asset swap with Statoil.</title>
<headline>BP says agrees North Sea asset swap with Statoil.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum Plc said on Thursday it had agreed to swap equity interests in North Sea fields with Norway's Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil).</p>
<p>BP will take over Statoil's share in the BP-operated Ula and Gyda fields and some of the Norwegian major's interest in the Draugen oilfield. In turn, BP will cede shares in the Jupiter, Glitne and Kvitebjorn fields to Statoil.</p>
</text>
